                    {
                        "sense_id": "45b588d2-cc13-39e6-8d91-f9156b6e55aa",
                        "entry_id": "7dc42f8d-b943-361a-92fc-96a956660f42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "First of all, before (some other specified thing)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bd0ae70-b698-486a-a524-a67818118593",
                                "sense_id": "45b588d2-cc13-39e6-8d91-f9156b6e55aa",
                                "text": "Consider what I erst have been and what thou seest me now:"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7de776f4-9385-3619-a1a4-11a5a92ac78d",
                        "entry_id": "7dc42f8d-b943-361a-92fc-96a956660f42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sooner (than); before."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4e9039a-e057-4a75-ad32-e28af3fc185a",
                                "sense_id": "7de776f4-9385-3619-a1a4-11a5a92ac78d",
                                "text": "Thenne he sente the varlet ageyne and bad hym telle Kyng Mark that I wille come as soone as I am hole / for erste I maye doo hym noo good\n\"Then he sent the varlet again, and bade him: Tell King Mark that I will come as soon as I am whole, for erst I may do him no good. \""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "385e0bb2-b2d3-36c4-9b92-b69859f8d7d6",
                        "entry_id": "7dc42f8d-b943-361a-92fc-96a956660f42",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Formerly, once, erstwhile."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f63c223-2f21-4686-8e60-5a7e64ef0352",
                                "sense_id": "385e0bb2-b2d3-36c4-9b92-b69859f8d7d6",
                                "text": "When lofty trees I see barren of leaves\nWhich erst from heat did canopy the herd"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
